# Docker build context filter for Shiro.
#
# IMPORTANT: Docker's ignore matching uses moby/patternmatcher, whose patterns
# are anchored to the CONTEXT ROOT. A bare `node_modules` only matches
# ./node_modules — it does NOT match apps/web/node_modules. Nested paths must
# therefore be given an explicit `**/` prefix.
#
# This matters a lot here: the host checkout contains
#   apps/web/.next            (~116 MB of stale build output)
#   apps/web/node_modules     (~86 symlinks pointing into ../../../node_modules/.pnpm)
#   packages/types/node_modules
# If they leak into the context, `COPY . .` in the builder stage overwrites the
# node_modules that the deps stage just installed with dangling symlinks into a
# .pnpm directory that was never copied. Verified with a port of
# moby/patternmatcher: bare patterns reported these as INCLUDED.

# --- dependencies (any depth) ---
**/node_modules

# --- build output (any depth) ---
**/.next
**/dist
**/out
**/tmp
**/temp
**/run

# --- env / secrets (any depth) ---
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.template

# --- pwa / generated service worker ---
sw.js
sw.js.*
workbox-*.js
workbox-*.js.*

# --- misc dev leftovers ---
pages/debug.tsx
pages/dev
patch/dist
release.zip
**/*.log
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# --- VCS / editor ---
.git
.gitignore
.github
.vscode
.drone.yml
renovate.json

# --- docs / meta (not needed to build) ---
CHANGELOG.md
ADDITIONAL_TERMS.md
SAY.md
NOTE.md
docs

# NOTE: the following MUST stay in the context — do not add them here:
#   patches/            pnpm patchedDependencies source; install fails without it
#   .npmrc              registry + hoist config
#   pnpm-lock.yaml      resolved dependency graph (also carries overrides/patches)
#   pnpm-workspace.yaml workspace definition
#   scripts/            build helper scripts
#   turbo.json          task pipeline
#   apps/web/public     static assets copied into the image
